  "title": "tribus Poblilia",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/tribus"
  ],
  "details": "<p><em>Tribus Poblilia</em> (<em>Poplilia</em>, <em>Publilia</em>) was the only one of the later rural tribes whose name derives from the Roman g<em>ens Popillia</em>, a well-known plebeian <em>nomen</em>. There are many indications about the location of the tribe that place it in either Volscian or Hernican territory.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Tribus Poblilia was a later rural tribe of Rome, which was established in 358 B.C.",
